    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing stolen base upside and favorable platoon splits to compensate for a few difficult pitching matchups. **Corbin Carroll** is our clear headliner today with a 76.31 efficiency score; facing Roupp (R) provides an ideal environment for his speed, and hitting out of the #2 hole ensures maximum opportunities to exploit that matchup. **Josh Naylor** also earns a strong recommendation at 64.71, as the significant pitching advantage against Kay (L) outweighs the minor park factor penalty. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** carries a 63.51 score into his matchup against Garrett (B); while he struggles against lefties, the extremely high xERA of the opposing starter (9.71) creates a massive offensive window that makes him an essential piece of our lineup.\n\nWe remain hyper-focused on SB potential, which keeps **Brice Turang** in the lineup at 56.74. While the SP skill matchup is slightly unfavorable, the combination of his #2 spot and the deliberate pace of the opposing pitcher makes him a prime candidate to test the catcher. Conversely, the benching of **Vinnie Pasquantino** at 41.44 was the tightest decision of the day; his projection tanked due to a poor platoon split against Suarez (L) and a low-leverage spot in the batting order. We are proceeding with caution regarding **James Wood** (51.22); despite his elite xwOBA, the matchup against a stingy pitcher with a quick release to the plate significantly limits his SB ceiling. Keep an eye on **Gabriel Moreno** and **Cole Young**, as both hover near our marginal floor; they remain active, but any late-game defensive substitutions or pinch-hit threats could lead to early exits.",
